{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e667be1e-ba51-40ba-aeae-9d8487c0cb31",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **Introduction to AI**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "053f6fcb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **Before we install anything: the vocabulary**\n",
    "\n",
    "Ten terms, one picture each. You will hear all of them from next week on.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **The model is a fixed function. The only thing you control is its input.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "235b6e60",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **1. Tokens**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_tokens.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Token** — a chunk of characters, the unit the model reads and writes.\n",
    "- Common words = 1 token; rare words, numbers and code split into many.\n",
    "- Everything is billed and limited in tokens, so token count = money."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "3f3fae03",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# pip install tiktoken\n",
    "import tiktoken\n",
    "\n",
    "enc = tiktoken.get_encoding(\"o200k_base\")      # vocabulary of recent OpenAI models\n",
    "\n",
    "text = \"The cluster's L_X = 3.2e44 erg/s\"\n",
    "ids = enc.encode(text)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(len(ids), \"tokens\")\n",
    "print([enc.decode([i]) for i in ids])\n",
    "print(ids)"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "d107f0e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# same meaning, very different price\n",
    "for s in [\"galaxy cluster\", \"kupa galaxii\", \"3.14159\", \"np.sqrt(2)\"]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{len(enc.encode(s)):>3} tokens   {s}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d6fffac6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **2. What the model does: guess the next token**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_next_token.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- The weights (~10¹¹ numbers) are **frozen** — nothing you say changes them.\n",
    "- **Temperature** — how adventurous the pick is; 0 = always the most likely token.\n",
    "- Each new token is appended and the whole thing runs again (**autoregression**).\n",
    "- **Hallucination** is not a bug: a plausible continuation is exactly what it was trained for."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "08e66100",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **3. Attention / the transformer**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_attention.png\" width=\"880\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Self-attention** — each token looks back at whichever earlier tokens matter.\n",
    "- 2017, [*Attention Is All You Need*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762) — replaced word-by-word RNNs;\n",
    "  **GPT** = Generative **Pre-trained Transformer**.\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"https://arxiv.org/html/1706.03762v7/Figures/ModalNet-21.png\" width=\"300\" style=\"display:block;margin:1em auto;\">"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "46c46f05",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **4. How a model is made**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_training_stages.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Pre-training** — next-token prediction on ~everything written; this is where the **knowledge\n",
    "  cutoff** comes from.\n",
    "- **Fine-tuning + RL** — turns a text-completer into an assistant; long RL gives **reasoning models**\n",
    "  (the `effort` knob below).\n",
    "- **You** — weights frozen, you only change the input. Fine-tuning your own model is almost never\n",
    "  worth it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "128d1374",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **5. Dense vs. Mixture-of-Experts**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_dense_vs_moe.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Dense** — every parameter runs for every token.\n",
    "- **MoE** — a router wakes a few experts: **total** parameters ≫ **active** parameters\n",
    "  (DeepSeek-V3: 671 B total, 37 B active).\n",
    "- Matters for local models: MoE needs the *memory* of a huge model but the *compute* of a small one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f3756381",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **6. Multimodality**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_multimodal.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- Images and audio become tokens in the same sequence as text.\n",
    "- So: paste a plot, a screenshot of a traceback, a photo of the whiteboard.\n",
    "- Images cost tokens too (~1–2 k for a screenshot). For figures, ask for **matplotlib code**, not an\n",
    "  image."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "06cf3164",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **7. Context window**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_context_window.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- Every call is **stateless** — a \"conversation\" is the client re-sending the whole history.\n",
    "- **Anything not in the context does not exist** for the model.\n",
    "- More is not better: junk in the context measurably degrades answers (*context rot*).\n",
    "- Choosing what goes in is the real skill — **context engineering**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ba77a2cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **8. Memory & RAG**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_memory.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- Session memory = the transcript; when it overflows it is **compacted** into a summary.\n",
    "- Long-term memory = a **file** (`AGENTS.md`, notes, your repo) that gets read back in.\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_rag.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- **RAG** — search your documents, paste the best chunks into the prompt. Good for papers and\n",
    "  manuals; for code, an agent with `grep` usually wins."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cba65dc3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **9. Tools (function calling)**\n",
    "\n",
    "A tool = a **JSON description** sent with the prompt + **your function** that does the work.\n",
    "\n",
    "```json\n",
    "{\"name\": \"calculate\",\n",
    " \"description\": \"Evaluate a mathematical expression. Use whenever an exact number is needed.\",\n",
    " \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\",\n",
    "                \"properties\": {\"expression\": {\"type\": \"string\"}},\n",
    "                \"required\": [\"expression\"]}}\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "- The model **cannot run anything** — it only emits *\"call `run_bash` with `{\"command\": \"ls\"}`\"*.\n",
    "  Your code decides whether to obey.\n",
    "- The description *is* a prompt: badly described tools are badly used.\n",
    "- **MCP** — an open standard for shipping tools as reusable servers (lecture 3).\n",
    "- Security is yours: a bash tool runs with your permissions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c3934c79",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **10. Agent**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_agent_loop.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Agent = model + tools + a loop**, running until it decides it is done.\n",
    "- The point is **feedback**: it can run the code, read the error, fix it, run again.\n",
    "- So always give it something to check against — a test, a plot, a known limit."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cc3bea56",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **11. Harness**\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"fig_harness.png\" width=\"950\" style=\"display:block;margin:1.2em auto;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- You rent the **model**; the **harness** is the program you install around it.\n",
    "- Codex CLI, Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor, Warp — same picture, different ergonomics.\n",
    "- The harness decides what the model sees and may do, so it matters as much as the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next week:** models and pricing, then we install one."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0ebf5ee1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **Glossary**\n",
    "\n",
    "| term | one line |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| token | chunk of characters the model reads and writes; ~4 characters |\n",
    "| weights / parameters | the ~10¹¹ frozen numbers that *are* the model |\n",
    "| temperature | how adventurous the sampling is; 0 = most likely token |\n",
    "| context window | everything the model can see in this one call |\n",
    "| context engineering | deciding what goes into that window |\n",
    "| system prompt | instructions placed at the top of the context |\n",
    "| knowledge cutoff | date after which the model has seen nothing |\n",
    "| hallucination | fluent, plausible, wrong — the default failure mode |\n",
    "| reasoning model | trained to think at length before answering |\n",
    "| dense / MoE | all parameters per token vs. a router picking a few experts |\n",
    "| multimodal | images and audio encoded as tokens too |\n",
    "| tool / function call | JSON description + your function; the model only *requests* it |\n",
    "| MCP | open standard for shipping tools as servers |\n",
    "| RAG | retrieve chunks from your documents, paste them into the prompt |\n",
    "| agent | model + tools + loop |\n",
    "| harness | the program that builds the context and runs the loop |\n",
    "| compaction | summarising an overflowing session so it fits again |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "Theory over — from here on, code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "71c9a323-8692-4910-bcee-b364d5261fcd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **OpenAI API**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "7087431b-39a3-43ae-90b4-af93bb54655c",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from openai import OpenAI\n",
    "\n",
    "# Put your API key here.\n",
    "# In a real application, use an environment variable or .env file instead.\n",
    "# API_KEY = \"YOUR_API_KEY_HERE\"\n",
    "API_KEY = API_KEY = open(\"/home/plsek/Documents/Keys/openai_aithenewhope_warp.txt\").read().strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "client = OpenAI(api_key=API_KEY)\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL = \"gpt-5.5\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6c701445-f508-4019-9dea-5f859c7f6ea3",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "A **star** is a single massive ball of hot gas/plasma that produces light and heat by nuclear fusion in its core.  \n",
      "- Example: **the Sun** is a star.\n",
      "\n",
      "A **galaxy** is a huge collection of many stars, along with gas, dust, planets, and dark matter, all held together by gravity.  \n",
      "- Example: **the Milky Way** is our galaxy, and it contains hundreds of billions of stars, including the Sun.\n",
      "\n",
      "So, the key difference is:\n",
      "\n",
      "**A star is one object; a galaxy is a vast system containing many stars.**\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "instructions = \"You are a helpful physics tutor. Explain concepts clearly and concisely.\"\n",
    "prompt = \"What is the difference between a star and a galaxy?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "response = client.responses.create(\n",
    "    model=MODEL,\n",
    "    instructions=instructions,\n",
    "    input=prompt\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(response.output_text)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "9f715273-500f-45a7-87d4-73225956cb20",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "A **star** is a single huge ball of hot gas/plasma that produces light and heat through **nuclear fusion** in its core.  \n",
       "- Example: **The Sun** is a star.\n",
       "\n",
       "A **galaxy** is an enormous system containing **billions or trillions of stars**, plus gas, dust, planets, and dark matter, all held together by gravity.  \n",
       "- Example: **The Milky Way** is our galaxy, and it contains the Sun.\n",
       "\n",
       "So the key difference is scale:\n",
       "\n",
       "**Star = one luminous object**  \n",
       "**Galaxy = a vast collection of many stars and other matter**"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
    "\n",
    "instructions=\"You are a helpful physics tutor. Explain concepts clearly and concisely.\"\n",
    "prompt = \"What is the difference between a star and a galaxy?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "stream = client.responses.create(\n",
    "    model=MODEL,\n",
    "    instructions=instructions,\n",
    "    input=prompt,\n",
    "    stream=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "output = display(Markdown(\"\"), display_id=True)\n",
    "text = \"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "for event in stream:\n",
    "    if event.type == \"response.output_text.delta\":\n",
    "        text += event.delta\n",
    "        output.update(Markdown(text))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d091373f-49b0-404c-b885-03f3b361afd9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **Simple chatbot**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "f7315a30-9c28-4f30-b0b3-70d0aa3285b1",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdin",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "You:  Hello\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Assistant: Hello! How can I help you today?\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdin",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "You:  Who is the president of USA?\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Assistant: The current president of the United States is **Donald J. Trump**.\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdin",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "You:  exit\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "conversation = []\n",
    "\n",
    "while True:\n",
    "    user_input = input(\"You: \")\n",
    "\n",
    "    if user_input.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n",
    "        break\n",
    "\n",
    "    conversation.append({\n",
    "        \"role\": \"user\",\n",
    "        \"content\": user_input\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "    response = client.responses.create(\n",
    "        model=MODEL,\n",
    "        instructions=\"You are a helpful and concise chatbot.\",\n",
    "        input=conversation\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"Assistant:\", response.output_text)\n",
    "\n",
    "    conversation.append({\n",
    "        \"role\": \"assistant\",\n",
    "        \"content\": response.output_text\n",
    "    })"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e31d4140-076c-4890-a63b-b28dcb1d345d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **Reasoning model**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "5e8c1968-698a-463a-8fa0-d2b73038fe30",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "### Reasoning\n",
       "\n",
       "**Estimating virial velocity**\n",
       "\n",
       "I need to help with estimating the characteristic virial velocity given a mass of \\(5e14\\) solar masses and a radius of \\(1\\) Mpc. Using the virial theorem, it looks like I can calculate \\(v\\) with \\(v \\sim \\sqrt{\\frac{GM}{R}}\\). I’ll convert everything to appropriate units: the mass becomes \\(9.945e44\\) kg, and the radius \\(3.086e22\\) m. After plugging in the values, I calculate a velocity of about \\(1467\\) km/s. This all assumes standard conditions, but I'll carefully explain each step for clarity!**Finalizing virial velocity calculation**\n",
       "\n",
       "I’m calculating the virial velocity with a radius of \\(1000\\) kpc. So, using the formula \\(v^2 = \\frac{GM}{R}\\), I plug in the values, getting \\(v^2 = 4.302e-6 \\times 5e14 / 1000\\), which simplifies to \\(2.151e6\\) \\((\\text{km/s})^2\\). Taking the square root gives me approximately \\(1467\\) km/s. It’s important I clarify that when applying the virial theorem, this velocity can also represent velocity dispersion. I’ll make sure my explanation is clear!"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "### Final answer\n",
       "\n",
       "Using the virial estimate,\n",
       "\n",
       "\\[\n",
       "v_{\\rm vir} \\sim \\sqrt{\\frac{GM}{R}}\n",
       "\\]\n",
       "\n",
       "with\n",
       "\n",
       "\\[\n",
       "M = 5\\times 10^{14}M_\\odot,\\qquad R = 1\\ \\text{Mpc}=1000\\ \\text{kpc}\n",
       "\\]\n",
       "\n",
       "and\n",
       "\n",
       "\\[\n",
       "G \\approx 4.30\\times 10^{-6}\\ \\frac{\\text{kpc}(\\text{km/s})^2}{M_\\odot},\n",
       "\\]\n",
       "\n",
       "we get\n",
       "\n",
       "\\[\n",
       "v_{\\rm vir} \\sim \\sqrt{\\frac{(4.30\\times 10^{-6})(5\\times 10^{14})}{1000}}\n",
       "\\]\n",
       "\n",
       "\\[\n",
       "v_{\\rm vir} \\sim \\sqrt{2.15\\times 10^6}\\ \\text{km/s}\n",
       "\\]\n",
       "\n",
       "\\[\n",
       "v_{\\rm vir} \\approx 1.5\\times 10^3\\ \\text{km/s}.\n",
       "\\]\n",
       "\n",
       "So the characteristic virial velocity is approximately\n",
       "\n",
       "\\[\n",
       "\\boxed{v_{\\rm vir} \\sim 1500\\ \\text{km/s}}\n",
       "\\]\n",
       "\n",
       "up to factors of order unity depending on the exact mass profile."
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
    "\n",
    "instructions = \"You are a physics tutor. Solve problems carefully and explain the important steps.\"\n",
    "prompt = \"A galaxy cluster has a total mass of 5e14 solar masses. Estimate its characteristic virial velocity assuming a radius of 1 Mpc.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "stream = client.responses.create(\n",
    "    model=\"gpt-5.5\",\n",
    "    instructions=instructions,\n",
    "    input=prompt,\n",
    "    reasoning={\"effort\": \"xhigh\",\n",
    "               \"summary\": \"detailed\"},\n",
    "    stream=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "reasoning = \"\"\n",
    "answer = \"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "reasoning_display = display(Markdown(\"### Reasoning\\n\"), display_id=True)\n",
    "answer_display = display(Markdown(\"### Final answer\\n\"), display_id=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "for event in stream:\n",
    "    # Reasoning summary\n",
    "    if event.type == \"response.reasoning_summary_text.delta\":\n",
    "        reasoning += event.delta\n",
    "        reasoning_display.update(Markdown(\"### Reasoning\\n\\n\" + reasoning))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Final answer\n",
    "    elif event.type == \"response.output_text.delta\":\n",
    "        answer += event.delta\n",
    "        answer_display.update(Markdown(\"### Final answer\\n\\n\" + answer))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62b2341a-2b9a-45d9-afc6-35ad09a0e823",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# **Simple AI agent**\n",
    "\n",
    "                 ┌──────────────┐\n",
    "                 │     User     │\n",
    "                 └──────┬───────┘\n",
    "                        │\n",
    "                        ▼\n",
    "                 ┌──────────────┐\n",
    "                 │     LLM      │\n",
    "                 └──────┬───────┘\n",
    "                        │\n",
    "              decides what to do\n",
    "                        │\n",
    "              ┌─────────┴─────────┐──────────────────┐\n",
    "              │                   │                  │\n",
    "              ▼                   ▼                  │\n",
    "       ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐          │\n",
    "       │  Calculator  │    │     Bash     │          │\n",
    "       │              │    │     Tool     │          │\n",
    "       └──────┬───────┘    └──────┬───────┘          │\n",
    "              │                   │                  │\n",
    "              └─────────┬─────────┘                  │ \n",
    "                        │                            │\n",
    "                        ▼                            │\n",
    "                 tool results                        │\n",
    "                        │                    answer directly\n",
    "                        ▼                            │\n",
    "                 ┌──────────────┐                    │\n",
    "                 │     LLM      │                    │\n",
    "                 └──────┬───────┘                    │\n",
    "                        │                            │\n",
    "               need another action?                  │\n",
    "                        │                            │\n",
    "              ┌─────────┴─────────┐                  │\n",
    "              │                   │                  │\n",
    "              │ yes               │ no               │\n",
    "              │                   │                  │\n",
    "              │                   ▼                  │\n",
    "              ▼            ┌──────────────┐          │\n",
    "      another tool call    │ final answer │──────────┘\n",
    "                           └──────────────┘"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
